{"name":"China Pink","hex":"#df6ea1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"china","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of porcelain, a hard white translucent ceramic made from kaolin, now  sometimes distinguished in reference to tableware as fine or good china.","Chinaware: porcelain tableware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/china"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dianthus chinensis","blocks":[{"text":"Dianthus chinensis, commonly known as rainbow pink or China pink, is a species of Dianthus native to northern China, Korea, Mongolia, and southeastern Russia. It is a herbaceous perennial plant growing to 30–50 cm tall."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Dianthus_chinensis_korea_2010.JPG/330px-Dianthus_chinensis_korea_2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dianthus_chinensis"},{"title":"China","blocks":[{"text":"China, officially the People's Republic of China (PRC), is a country in East Asia. It is divided into 33 province-level divisions, including two special administrative regions. Beijing is the capital, while Shanghai is the most populous city by urban area. Its geography features the Central Plain, major rivers such as the Yangtze and Yellow River, deserts, subtropical and temperate forests, plateaus, and mountain ranges such as the Himalayas. It is the world's second-most populous country after India, with a population exceeding 1.4 billion. Covering 9.6 million square kilometers (3,700,000 sq mi), it is the third largest country by area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg/330px-Flag_of_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg/120px-Dianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg/250px-Dianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Dianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg/120px-Dianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADianthus_chinensis_Blanco1.94b-cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Flore_des_Serres_v13_011a.jpg/120px-Flore_des_Serres_v13_011a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Flore_des_Serres_v13_011a.jpg/250px-Flore_des_Serres_v13_011a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"ht